{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"c1","type":"claim","text":"The flat's situation can be posed as an institutional-design problem — three people with unstable schedules and plausibly divergent cleanliness standards governing shared space by repeated informal consensus is inherently high-friction — rather than primarily as a failure to record or clarify agreements.","scope":"The household described in the task","bearing":"If accepted, effort should go toward reducing how much must be agreed, not only toward improving the agreements.","mentions":["p.rival.0"]},{"id":"o1","type":"objection","text":"The conjecture that most of this class of argument disappears once agreements are recorded with explicit done-criteria is contestable: written terms relocate disputes from recall to interpretation, exception-handling, and enforcement, and they create a maintainer/enforcer role that commonly falls on the system's proposer and curdles into perceived nagging.","target":["p.rival.0"],"grounds":"Recurring 'what the agreement meant' disputes are also what self-serving interpretation and standards gaps produce; the reference engages the account's visible body, since its commitment records were not supplied.","bearing":"Lowers the expected yield of the written-agreement trial without reducing it to zero; genuinely recall-driven disputes would still disappear."},{"id":"o2","type":"objection","text":"Reading the avoiding friend's withdrawal mainly as cost-sensitivity to conversation format under-reads it: exit from negotiations the friend keeps losing, or from a standards argument they cannot win, fits the same facts, and an asynchronous channel still requires the friend to opt in.","target":["p.rival.0"],"bearing":"Redesigns premised on re-including the avoider may fail silently; systems that tolerate non-participation are less fragile."},{"id":"c2","type":"claim","text":"Long-stretch exclusive ownership zones judged by outcome, or rotating whole weeks of total responsibility, shrink the coordination surface: fewer points at which disagreement about meaning can arise, schedule churn absorbed inside the owner's or duty-week holder's own planning, and no attendance requirement for the withdrawing friend.","consequence":"A recurring negotiation cost becomes a one-time assignment cost plus occasional rebalancing; initial assignment of unequal domains can be made fairer by turn-picking or credit-bidding."},{"id":"c3","type":"claim","text":"If the recurring argument tracks a standards gap — whether chores need doing at all, or to what level — clarity about wording cannot settle it, only expose it; resolution then runs through decoupling, where the higher-standard member performs or funds the difference.","mentions":["p.rival.0"],"bearing":"Extends the account's own caution that clarity is not fairness into a different remedy class."},{"id":"u1","type":"use","text":"Retain, as compatible with the rival reframing: raising the pattern rather than the latest incident at a calm scheduled moment, and the closing flag that refusal across all channels changes the question from chore management to the viability of the living arrangement. Because the account's commitment field was not supplied, this uptake engages its published body as a whole rather than specific records.","target":["p.rival.0"]},{"id":"m1","type":"commitment","action":"Propose a domain-ownership or weekly full-rotation trial with turn-picking or credit-bidding for the unequal initial split; trial paying for a cleaner if budget allows; if neither friend will convene, the asker unilaterally declares and holds their own scope — which chores they will own and which they will stop silently covering.","scope":"Next two to four weeks","consequence":"Visible lapses may escalate short-term conflict and reopen negotiation via the lapse rather than a meeting; the unilateral version fails if the asker cannot tolerate undone chores longer than the others can.","depends":["c2"]},{"id":"m2","type":"commitment","action":"Run a minimal written record — one shared line per agreement for two weeks — purely as a diagnostic instrument, not as the proposed fix.","consequence":"If disputes cease, recall was the driver and the first account's fuller system is indicated; if disputes persist in mutated form (what counts, exceptions, tone), ownership, rotation, or decoupling is indicated instead.","depends":["o1"],"mentions":["p.rival.0"]},{"id":"q1","type":"problem","text":"Which underlying cause obtains — recall divergence, interest conflict, or a standards gap — is not established by the task material; the diagnostic in m2 discriminates only if all three flatmates produce at least some agreements worth recording during the trial."},{"id":"q2","type":"problem","text":"Ownership relocates rather than abolishes negotiation: the initial split of unequal domains must itself be agreed by people currently failing to agree. Whether one structured one-time conversation succeeds where repeated informal ones failed is unresolved; turn-picking and bidding are proposed to lower its temperature, not guaranteed to."}],"uptake":["c1","o1","o2","c2","c3","u1","m1","m2","q1","q2"]}